ANSWER: {"completedSection": "Equipment covered: CMMs, micrometers, gauge blocks, torque wrenches. Calibration intervals: CMMs - annually, micrometers - biannually, gauge blocks - quarterly, torque wrenches - monthly. Traceability requirements: All calibrations must be traceable to national or international standards. Out-of-tolerance actions: Any equipment found out-of-tolerance must be re-calibrated immediately and any measurements taken since the last calibration must be reviewed. Identification methods: All calibrated equipment must be clearly marked with calibration dates and due dates. Records: Calibration records must be maintained and readily available for review, including dates, performed by, due dates, and results.

", "references": "ISO 17025, ISO 9001:2015, ASME B89.6.3, ISO 376", "clauseAlignment": "This procedure aligns with ISO 9001 clause 7.1.5 by ensuring that monitoring and measuring resources are calibrated or verified at specified intervals, have traceability to national or international standards, and that records are maintained. Out-of-tolerance actions and identification methods are specified to maintain the validity of previous measurements and to ensure equipment can be easily identified and its calibration status determined.

